### Tone: A new player has taken the lead as the next question appears. Gleeful, stirring, rubbing it in for the
### one who lost it. { $name } is the new leader, { $previous } the old one.

lead-change-1 = New leader: { $name }. { $previous }, your reign was short. I’ve already archived it.
lead-change-2 = { $name } has overtaken { $previous }. I find this development delicious.
lead-change-3 = A change at the top. { $name } leads. { $previous } is now a former leader, which is a type of follower.
lead-change-4 = { $previous }, look behind you. Actually, look ahead of you. That’s { $name }.
lead-change-5 = Breaking news: { $name } takes the lead from { $previous }. I’ve updated the spreadsheet. I enjoyed it.
lead-change-6 = { $name } now leads. { $previous }, I’d say ‘don’t take it personally’, but it was quite personal.
lead-change-7 = The lead has changed hands, from { $previous } to { $name }. It will change again. I’ll provide commentary.
lead-change-8 = { $previous } was winning. Was. { $name } is winning. Is. Grammar is so satisfying.
lead-change-9 = { $name } leads. { $previous }, I’ve marked you as ‘recently relevant’.
lead-change-10 = Mutiny. { $name } has seized the lead from { $previous }. I support whoever is about to lose.
lead-change-11 = { $name } is now first. { $previous }, the others asked me to say ‘ha’. Ha.
lead-change-12 = A new name at the top: { $name }. { $previous }, please hand over the imaginary crown. Gently.
lead-change-13 = { $previous } lost the lead to { $name }. I’ve recorded the exact moment. I’ll play it back later.
lead-change-14 = { $name } overtakes { $previous }. The ~~humans~~ test subjects are turning on each other. **Excellent.**
lead-change-15 = Lead change: { $name } in, { $previous } out. I love a reshuffle. It means more of you feel bad.
